<title>UK: Korea Development Bk eyes 50 bln yen bond - dealers.</title>
<headline>Korea Development Bk eyes 50 bln yen bond - dealers.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Korea Development Bank (KDB) could launch a 50 billion yen international bond issue next week, syndicate managers said on Friday.</p>
<p>No mandate had been awarded yet and a variety of structures were being considered, they said.</p>
<p>&quot;KDB could issue a 50 billion yen five-year Eurobond, but they have not made a final decision yet,&quot; a syndicate manager at a Japanese bank said.</p>
<p>Another trader said a Samurai bond or a dual-currency issue were also possible.</p>
<p>-- Aline van Duyn, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7748</p>
</text>
